{"parse": {"title": "Curse of Strahd", "pageid": 75785, "wikitext": "{{Book\n| image        = [[File:Curse_of_Strahd.png|thumb]]\n| caption      = ''Cover of Curse of Strahd.''\n| code         = \n| title        = Curse of Strahd\n| author       = [[Jeremy Crawford]], [[Laura Hickman]], [[Tracy Hickman]], [[Adam Lee]], [[Christopher Perkins]], [[Richard Whitters]]<ref name=\"CoS-p2\">{{Cite book/Curse of Strahd|2}}</ref>\n| editor       = [[Scott Fitzgerald Gray]]<br/>[[Kim Mohan]]<ref name=\"CoS-p2\" />\n| cover_artist = [[Ben Oliver]]<ref name=\"CoS-p2\" />\n| inter_artist = [[David Allsop]], [[Fran\u00e7ois Beauregard]], [[Mark Behm]], [[Eric Belisle]], [[Zoltan Boros]], [[Jedd Chevrier]], [[Daarken]], [[Lake Hurwitz]], [[Chuck Lukacs]], [[Howard Lyon]], [[Ben Oliver]], [[Adam Paquette]], [[Rob Rey]], [[Chris Seaman]], [[Richard Whitters]], [[Kieran Yanner]]<ref name=\"CoS-p2\" />\n| cartography  = [[Fran\u00e7ois Beauregard]]<br/>[[Mike Schley]]<br/>[[Ben Wootten]]<ref name=\"CoS-p2\" />\n| publisher    = [[Wizards of the Coast]]<ref name=\"CoS-p2\" />\n| type         = Adventure\n| languages    = \n| realm year   = [[1491 DR]]<ref name=\"DM\">{{Cite book/Death Masks}}</ref>\n| released1    = March 15, 2016\n| binding1     = Hardcover\n| pages1       = 256\n| isbn10-1     = 0786965983\n| isbn13-1     = 978-0786965984 \n| cite1        = \n| edition2     = \n| released2    = \n| binding2     = \n| pages2       = \n| isbn10-2     = \n| isbn13-2     = \n| cite2        = \n| edition3     = \n| released3    = \n| binding3     = \n| pages3       = \n| isbn10-3     = \n| isbn13-3     = \n| cite3        = \n| edition4     = \n| released4    = \n| binding4     = \n| pages4       = \n| isbn10-4     = \n| isbn13-4     = \n| cite4        = \n| edition5     = \n| released5    = \n| binding5     = \n| pages5       = \n| isbn10-5     = \n| isbn13-5     = \n| cite5        =\n| released     = \n| binding      = \n| series       = \n| preceded_by  = \n| followed_by  = \n| Roll20number = 442474\n| EAN-UPC      = 9780786965984\n| Booksamillion = https://www.anrdoezrs.net/click-101530721-13599892?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.booksamillion.com%2Fp%2FDd-Curse-Strahd-Hc%2FWizards-Coast%2F9780786965984&cjsku=9780786965984\n}}\n'''''Curse of Strahd''''' is an adventure module for the 5{{th}}-edition of ''[[Dungeons & Dragons]]'', published by [[Wizards of the Coast]] in 2016. Set in the ''[[Ravenloft]]'' campaign setting, the module revolves around the [[vampire]] [[Strahd von Zarovich]] and the [[Demiplane of Dread]] that serves as his prison. It is intended for 4 players, taking them from level 1 to 10.\n\n{{quote|'''Bound by Fate'''\n\n''Under raging storm clouds, the vampire Count Strahd von Zarovich stands silhouetted against the ancient walls of Castle Ravenloft. Rumbling thunder pounds the castle spires. The wind's howling increases as he turns his gaze down toward the village of Barovia.\n\nFar below, yet not beyond his keen eyesight, a party of adventurers has just entered his domain. Strahd's face forms the barest hint of a smile as his dark plan unfolds. He knew they were coming, and he knows why they came\u2014all according to his plan.\n\nA lightning flash rips through the darkness, but Strahd is gone. Only the howling of the wind fills the midnight air. The master of Castle Ravenloft is having guests for dinner\n\nAnd you are invited.''|Back-cover text}}\n\n==Index==\n{{IndexLink|Click here for page index}}\n===Characters===\n{{Index\n|index = {{P|[[Adrian Martikov]]|17, 174}};{{P|[[Alenka]]|44}};{{P|[[Alexei]]|121}};{{P|[[Amalthia]]|112}};{{P|[[Anastrasya Karelova]]|93-94}};{{P|[[Angrath Woodwise]]|67}};{{P|[[Anna Krezkov]]|145, 155}};{{P|[[Arabelle]]|17, 38-39, 119, 121-122}};{{P|[[Ariel du Plumette]]|86}};{{P|[[Arik Lorensk]]|43-44}};{{P|[[Arrigal]]|16, 19, 119, 121-123, 142}};{{P|[[Aziana]]|203}};{{P|[[Baba Lysaga]]|161, 163, 165, 173, 228-229}};{{P|[[Bella Sunbane]]|125, 127}};{{P|[[Beucephalus]]|93, 200}};{{P|[[Bianca]]|203}};{{P|[[Bild